ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Teeth that are previously restored or have caries\n-  Patients who have orthodontic treatment\n-  Patients who are not cooperative for the dental procedure\n-  Teeth that have dental flourosis or enamel malformation according to the specific syndromes\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Teeth that are previously restored",\n                  "Procedure": [\n                    "restored"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure-Name": [\n                    "restored"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Comparison": [\n                    "previously"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                    "previously"\n                  ],\n                  "Modifier": [\n                    "Teeth"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "raw_text": "or have caries",\n                  "Condition": [\n                    "caries"\n                  ],\n                  "Condition-Name": [\n                    "caries"\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "- Patients who have orthodontic treatment",\n              "Procedure": [\n                "orthodontic treatment"\n              ],\n              "Procedure-Name": [\n                "orthodontic treatment"\n              ]\n