ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Federated boxers with lumbar injury with medical diagnosis\n-  Who are or have been treated by pharmacological or physiotherapy in the last 6 months\n-  Presenting allergies or alterations of the skin\n-  Not sign the informed consent document.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Federated boxers",\n                  "Observation": [\n                    "Federated boxers"\n                  ],\n                  "Observation-Name": [\n                    "Federated boxers"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "raw_text": "with lumbar injury with medical diagnosis",\n                  "Modifier": [\n                    "lumbar"\n                  ],\n                  "Observation": [\n                    "injury"\n                  ],\n                  "Observation-Name": [\n                    "injury"\n                  ],\n                  "Provider": [\n                    "medical"\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "OR": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Who are or have been treated by pharmacological",\n                  "Procedure": [\n                    "treated"\n                  ],\n                  "Modifier": [\n                    "pharmacological"\n                  ]\n                },\n