ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Patient over the age of 18, patient with an anus fistula with indication for surgical treatment\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "raw_text": "- Patient over the age of 18, patient with an anus fistula",\n      "Condition": [\n        "anus fistula"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Name": [\n        "anus fistula"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Value": [\n        "18"\n      ],\n      "Age": [\n        "age"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Comparison": [\n        "over the age of 18"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Operator": [\n        "over"\n      ]\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "raw_text": "with indication for surgical treatment",\n      "Procedure": [\n        "surgical treatment"\n      ],\n      "Procedure-Name": [\n        "surgical treatment"\n      ],\n      "Indication": [\n        "indication"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}<|eot_id|>']
